<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="VirtDeck.Avalonia.Views.Containers.HubAccountMenu">

  <!--
    A Menu holding one item, not a Button with a flyout, for the reason the console's toolbar is a
    Menu: JbTopLevelMenuItem already draws the flat cell, the chevron, the open-and-stay-pressed
    state and a popup framed like a context menu, and the Menu theme wires the two together through
    its ItemContainerTheme. There is nothing here to template.

    MinHeight and Padding drop the theme's toolbar figures (22 and 9,3): the cell stretches to the
    whole height of the status bar and its hover covers the strip top to bottom, which is what a
    status bar widget does and what a toolbar's pill does not. The 10px either side of the label is
    this cell's own, and that is the point of writing it here rather than leaving it to the bar: the
    same gap as the bar's border padding, but **inside** the hover, so the highlight reaches the
    window edge instead of stopping short of it with a dead strip beside it. MainWindow's status bar
    cancels its own padding under this slot and drops the separator's margin on this side to pay for
    it, so the label sits exactly where it did.

    The Menu itself stays enabled and carries the tooltip while the item inside it is disabled: a
    disabled control is not hit-testable in Avalonia, so a reason hung off the item would never be
    read. Same arrangement as CheckRow's border and ServiceRow's autostart tick.
  -->
  <Menu Name="MenuHost" VerticalAlignment="Stretch">
    <MenuItem Name="AccountItem" MinHeight="0" Padding="10,0" VerticalAlignment="Stretch">
      <MenuItem.Header>
        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="5">
          <!-- Head and shoulders, the app's own: the whole account of how it is drawn is in
               MainWindow.axaml, where it names the user accounts module. A size down from the 16
               it wears there, to sit beside 12pt status text rather than a menu label. -->
          <Path Data="M8,2 A2.75,2.75 0 1 1 8,7.5 A2.75,2.75 0 1 1 8,2 Z M2.5,14 A5.5,5.5 0 0 1 8,9.5 A5.5,5.5 0 0 1 13.5,14"
                Width="14" Height="14" Stretch="Uniform" StrokeThickness="1.2"
                Stroke="{Binding $parent[MenuItem].Foreground}"
                VerticalAlignment="Center" />
          <TextBlock Name="AccountLabel" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        </StackPanel>
      </MenuItem.Header>

      <MenuItem Name="LoginItem" Header="Log in" />
      <MenuItem Name="LogoutItem" Header="Log out" />
    </MenuItem>
  </Menu>
</UserControl>
